(987681, 115781, 22556, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by rachelr_ph:</b></div><hr/><i> picture gives an idea and a feeling of emptiness and the dawn in the horizon gives an idea of hope. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Youre rigth rachel</td>', 'Originally posted by rachelr_ph: picture gives an idea and a feeling of emptiness and the dawn in the horizon gives an idea of hope.   Youre rigth rachel', '2004-11-03 00:57:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(987683, 115379, 26849, '<td valign="top">Since this photo has the highest comments so far, I thought I would give a general response to the comments.<br/> <br/>I felt because of the nature of the topic that not showing the face would show more respect for the person. I did have another shot with his legs but rejected because it revealed too much of the face.<br/> <br/>It had been raining just hours before, which explains the less than bright lighting. It''s a little soft because this was a hand held shot while in my car at the stop sign near the recycling center.<br/> <br/>I agree that the image is very cluttered, and the original was worse. This is why I cropped tight yet it still tells the story. I attempt to tell the story as if I could not add the title.<br/> <br/>The levels were adjusted for more saturation on the red and blue to help separate the forground objects from the background, and the yellow was partially desaturated to make those yellow posts fade a bit. Because the  jacket got so much attention I may have added too much saturation.<br/> <br/>The surprise to me was when editing, I noticed he only has one hand, thus the title reference.<br/> <br/>Left in only enough of the sign to tell the story. <br/> <br/>Thanks again for all the comments.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Since this photo has the highest comments so far, I thought I would give a general response to the comments. I felt because of the nature of the topic that not showing the face would show more respect for the person. I did have another shot with his legs but rejected because it revealed too much of the face. It had been raining just hours before, which explains the less than bright lighting. It''s a little soft because this was a hand held shot while in my car at the stop sign near the recycling center. I agree that the image is very cluttered, and the original was worse. This is why I cropped tight yet it still tells the story. I attempt to tell the story as if I could not add the title. The levels were adjusted for more saturation on the red and blue to help separate the forground objects from the background, and the yellow was partially desaturated to make those yellow posts fade a bit. Because the  jacket got so much attention I may have added too much saturation. The surprise to me was when editing, I noticed he only has one hand, thus the title reference. Left in only enough of the sign to tell the story.  Thanks again for all the comments. ', '2004-11-03 00:58:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(987711, 115172, 8759, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your first ribbon Good job!</td>', 'Congrats on your first ribbon Good job!', '2004-11-03 01:14:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(987726, 115415, 20056, '<td valign="top">Because of my previous picture I decided to put more light this time... craso error; I should have used another kind of lighting.<br/> <br/>Thanks for all your comments!<br/>P.S. Do You want to buy some painting ?</td>', 'Because of my previous picture I decided to put more light this time... craso error; I should have used another kind of lighting. Thanks for all your comments!P.S. Do You want to buy some painting ?', '2004-11-03 01:19:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(987734, 115611, 8759, '<td valign="top">Sorry it didn''t score better. Might be the "don''t meet the challenge"<br/>Mie mi-a placut ca poza si i-am dat numai 6 pentru motivul sus mentionat. Tibi</td>', 'Sorry it didn''t score better. Might be the "don''t meet the challenge"Mie mi-a placut ca poza si i-am dat numai 6 pentru motivul sus mentionat. Tibi', '2004-11-03 01:22:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(987742, 115077, 8759, '<td valign="top">Congrats in your first ribbon. <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-03 01:26:39.</i></td>', 'Congrats in your first ribbon. ', '2004-11-03 01:25:05.000000', '2004-11-03 01:26:39.000000', 0),
(987787, 115695, 27440, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for voting on me :) <br/> <br/>I am really happy with the score :)<br/>I was expecting a middle score in the staff somewhere around 60-90. <br/>I knew people would send photographs of people on the streets or people begging, but I thought that this was to obvious, so I wanted to do something a bit else. Congratulations to all entrys in this chalange :)<br/> <br/>Can''t wait what the critique club will say :P<br/> <br/>Sorry for my spelling and grammar mistakes!</td>', 'Thank you all for voting on me :)  I am really happy with the score :)I was expecting a middle score in the staff somewhere around 60-90. I knew people would send photographs of people on the streets or people begging, but I thought that this was to obvious, so I wanted to do something a bit else. Congratulations to all entrys in this chalange :) Can''t wait what the critique club will say :P Sorry for my spelling and grammar mistakes!', '2004-11-03 01:51:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(987802, 115077, 26151, '<td valign="top">Wow, a bittersweet victory. After I took the photo--and got over the guilt of actually taking it--and thought about the challenge, I knew it would be a powerful entry. I figured top 20, maybe top 10. I never thought ribbon until the votes and comments started coming in.<br/> <br/>Thank you to everyone for your great comments.<br/> <br/>Hopefully I can win a ribbon in a less opportunist, and more fun challenge. As you can see from my other entries, I still have a lot to learn about photography. I just happened to be in the right place at the right time for this challenge. Thailand is a beautiful country, but it is riddled with poverty. There were so many pictures I could have taken that would have been equally or even more powerful than this one. It''s not all bad though, there is a lot of affluance and beauty there too. And most of the people there were very nice and helpful.<br/> <br/>BTW, I''m back home now.<br/> <br/>Thank you,<br/> <br/>Mark<br/> <br/>edited for spelling<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-03 02:06:28.</i></td>', 'Wow, a bittersweet victory. After I took the photo--and got over the guilt of actually taking it--and thought about the challenge, I knew it would be a powerful entry. I figured top 20, maybe top 10. I never thought ribbon until the votes and comments started coming in. Thank you to everyone for your great comments. Hopefully I can win a ribbon in a less opportunist, and more fun challenge. As you can see from my other entries, I still have a lot to learn about photography. I just happened to be in the right place at the right time for this challenge. Thailand is a beautiful country, but it is riddled with poverty. There were so many pictures I could have taken that would have been equally or even more powerful than this one. It''s not all bad though, there is a lot of affluance and beauty there too. And most of the people there were very nice and helpful. BTW, I''m back home now. Thank you, Mark edited for spelling', '2004-11-03 02:04:04.000000', '2004-11-03 02:06:28.000000', 0),
(987816, 115172, 26669, '<td valign="top">Hey All,<br/>Thanks for all the great comments, After the first two challenge entries i submited i took onboard the help ful comments and applied to this shot. Lets hope this is the start of a small collection of ribbons for the S7000 team and for us here in Ireland.<br/> <br/>Congrats to 1st and 2nd placing.<br/> <br/>Again thanks for the kind comments<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-03 03:20:06.</i></td>', 'Hey All,Thanks for all the great comments, After the first two challenge entries i submited i took onboard the help ful comments and applied to this shot. Lets hope this is the start of a small collection of ribbons for the S7000 team and for us here in Ireland. Congrats to 1st and 2nd placing. Again thanks for the kind comments', '2004-11-03 02:29:07.000000', '2004-11-03 03:20:06.000000', 0),
(987818, 115611, 14257, '<td valign="top">Tanks for your vote! The only changes that I made at my image were to increase the luminance and a bit the contrast.<br/>When this idea come on my mind, I searched in dictionary and I found this: 3.Unproductiveness; infertility: the poverty of the soil. (From dictionary.com)<br/>In this case, I thing the image was on the challenge theme.<br/></td>', 'Tanks for your vote! The only changes that I made at my image were to increase the luminance and a bit the contrast.When this idea come on my mind, I searched in dictionary and I found this: 3.Unproductiveness; infertility: the poverty of the soil. (From dictionary.com)In this case, I thing the image was on the challenge theme.', '2004-11-03 02:29:46.000000', NULL, 0),
