(988009, 114351, 23478, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all of the comments.  This man is an interesting story, I have known him for several years.  At one point, I tried to help him move out of his situation and into some permanent housing through a non-profit organization in the area, but he was too used to his way of life.  To me, his face reads of all the wear and tear associated with the dificulties that poverty brings.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-03 04:40:50.</i></td>', 'Thanks for all of the comments.  This man is an interesting story, I have known him for several years.  At one point, I tried to help him move out of his situation and into some permanent housing through a non-profit organization in the area, but he was too used to his way of life.  To me, his face reads of all the wear and tear associated with the dificulties that poverty brings.', '2004-11-03 04:39:02.000000', '2004-11-03 04:40:50.000000', 0),
(988016, 115781, 24642, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your 2nd best.  You are definitely on the right track developing your emotional and creative style.</td>', 'Congrats on your 2nd best.  You are definitely on the right track developing your emotional and creative style.', '2004-11-03 04:49:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(988070, 114810, 22125, '<td valign="top">CONGRATULATIONS BOB, Not a bad pic but.Can''t see much poverty in it though. lol</td>', 'CONGRATULATIONS BOB, Not a bad pic but.Can''t see much poverty in it though. lol', '2004-11-03 06:10:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(988113, 115018, 25371, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone who voted and droped a comment.</td>', 'Thanks to everyone who voted and droped a comment.', '2004-11-03 06:41:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(988119, 114766, 20836, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for your encouraging messages, specialy for those to whom tho photo spokes.<br/>I deliberately refuse send a picture of a single person showing is misery and prefered send one where external signs could show the poverty some people live with.<br/>Post-editing was only crop, adjust brightness and contrast, add an unsharp mask, all whith PSP CS.</td>', 'Thank you all for your encouraging messages, specialy for those to whom tho photo spokes.I deliberately refuse send a picture of a single person showing is misery and prefered send one where external signs could show the poverty some people live with.Post-editing was only crop, adjust brightness and contrast, add an unsharp mask, all whith PSP CS.', '2004-11-03 06:56:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(988123, 114387, 18191, '<td valign="top">Sorry about this...I probably should have ewntered this into Free Study. Unfortunately, I was blind to realize that the story could not really be read just by the photograph alone. I thought it would have been alright for the viewer to draw their own conclusions. The hope here has to do with hte neglegent family that I got into a conversation with him about after meeting him in the projects of the town that I live in. When I told him about DPC and about what I wanted to take his photo for; he became intrigued and he said he always loved photography. I let him try out my camera and he was so amazed. He said that whenever he went to his friends'' houses, that they would have their parents get him a disposable camera and that he''d take it home and hide it and use it and his friends would then develop it. This story really hit me pretty deep. He had a tough life, but he still enjoyed life''s comfort. This is why I was comfortable in using this photograph for poverty. Poverty does not always need to mean poor and sad and unkempt and disgruntled, to me and to Kojo it meant something a little bit different. Hope this helps...<br/>Lee</td>', 'Sorry about this...I probably should have ewntered this into Free Study. Unfortunately, I was blind to realize that the story could not really be read just by the photograph alone. I thought it would have been alright for the viewer to draw their own conclusions. The hope here has to do with hte neglegent family that I got into a conversation with him about after meeting him in the projects of the town that I live in. When I told him about DPC and about what I wanted to take his photo for; he became intrigued and he said he always loved photography. I let him try out my camera and he was so amazed. He said that whenever he went to his friends'' houses, that they would have their parents get him a disposable camera and that he''d take it home and hide it and use it and his friends would then develop it. This story really hit me pretty deep. He had a tough life, but he still enjoyed life''s comfort. This is why I was comfortable in using this photograph for poverty. Poverty does not always need to mean poor and sad and unkempt and disgruntled, to me and to Kojo it meant something a little bit different. Hope this helps...Lee', '2004-11-03 06:58:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(988128, 114785, 16493, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your personal best.<br/>Only minor things, mostly setup that would make this picture realy take of. <br/>Good idea and well executed.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-03 07:10:06.</i></td>', 'Congratulations on your personal best.Only minor things, mostly setup that would make this picture realy take of. Good idea and well executed.', '2004-11-03 07:08:11.000000', '2004-11-03 07:10:06.000000', 0),
